-- Lean-only: no Rocq source. A Lean-only helper of `BudgetWitness.lean`.
import {{unit_prefix}}.BudgetWit.Rzb
import {{package}}.Reusable.YP0n
import {{package}}.Reusable.YP03
import {{package}}.Reusable.YP04
import {{package}}.Reusable.YN35

/-! The `realizes` lemmas of R1's `Reusable/YP0n.lean`, `YP03.lean`, `YP04.lean` and
`YN35.lean` that the driver's usage path uses, restated over `Rzb.rzb`.

Each declaration mirrors the R1 declaration named in its doc comment: its name is the R1 name
with `rz_` written `rzb_` and `realizes_` written `rzb_` (or `_b` appended when the name has
neither), its statement is the R1 statement with `realizes` written `rzb`, and its proof is the
R1 proof with the mirrored lemmas renamed. Where R1 builds a node, the proof also gives
`grant_ok` for it: `grant_ok_no … 96 …` at `set_tid_address` (`rzb_set_tid_first`).

Two statements differ from the mirror rule. R1's `rz_chk1_silent` and
`rz_ret_only_copyins_silent` take no `node_ok`, but build a node at a syscall whose number they
do not fix, so their hypotheses do not give `grant_ok`; `rzb_chk1_silent` and
`rzb_ret_only_copyins_silent` take `grant_ok segs (config.mkCfg (pend_at regs pc mem rom) model)`
as an extra hypothesis right after their `check_syscall` hypothesis. Their caller on the usage
path (`WritevG`'s mirror of `YN3g.rz_writev_empty`) has `bv_unsigned (getr regs 17) = 66` and
discharges it with `grant_ok_no`.

Private helpers copied from `YP0n.lean` (used by `rzb_chk1_silent`'s proof):
`yp0n_checked_table_arms`, `yp0n_agree`.

Each part opens the namespaces its R1 file opens, so each proof elaborates in R1's scope. -/

namespace {{unit_prefix}}.BudgetWit.RunB
open {{package}}.Reusable.YK15
open {{package}}.Reusable.R.Cfg
open {{unit_prefix}}.BudgetWit.Rzb

section Addr
-- The section is empty: this file states no fact about the target's binary; 96 is the RISC-V
-- Linux number of set_tid_address, and the stop address is `YN35.SRC1_STDIO_WRITE`.
end Addr

/-! ## `YP0n.lean` -/

section YP0nPart

open {{package}}.Reusable.YP0n

/-- Copied from `YP0n.lean:159` (private there). -/
/-- Copied from `YP0n.lean:164` (private there). -/
/-- `YP0n.rz_chk1_silent` (`YP0n.lean:462`), with `grant_ok` for the pending configuration
after the `check_syscall` hypothesis. -/
    grant_ok segs (config.mkCfg (pend_at regs pc mem rom) model) →
  intro regs pc mem rom model eff m' T Hh Hlz Hok Hg Hh' Hlz' Huniq Hc
  refine rzb_silent1 segs _
    (config.mkCfg (advance_past_svc (apply_effect (pend_at regs pc mem rom) eff)) m') T ?_ Hg ?_
/-- `YP0n.rz_ret_only_copyins_silent` (`YP0n.lean:563`), with `grant_ok` for the pending
configuration after the `check_syscall` hypothesis. -/
    grant_ok segs (config.mkCfg (pend_at regs pc mem rom) model) →
  intro regs pc mem rom model reads r m' T Hh Hlz Hchk Hg Hh' Hlz' Hc
  refine rzb_chk1_silent segs regs pc mem rom model (with_copyins reads (mkEffect r [] [])) m' T
    Hh Hlz ?_ Hg Hh' Hlz' ?_ ?_
/-- `YP0n.rz_exit_at` (`YP0n.lean:583`). -/
/-- `YP0n.rz_exit_small` (`YP0n.lean:593`). -/
/-- `YP0n.rz_set_tid_first` (`YP0n.lean:641`); the node's `grant_ok` is `grant_ok_no … 96 …`. -/
    ⟨Z_to_bv 64 1, H1⟩ T ?_
    (grant_ok_no segs (pend_at regs pc mem rom) model (getr regs 17) 96 rfl Hno (by decide)
      (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)) ?_
end YP0nPart

